WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Radiation and magnetic fields

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Four radiation environments

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:16.800
Dose rates measured on the ISS and on the lunar surface by Chang'e-4, a deep-space estimate, and a modelled solar particle event of 150 mGy. Colours show radiation damage in each cell.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:28.100
By 72 h: 0.86 mGy on the ISS, 152 mGy with the solar particle event.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:38.800
Yet all four seedlings are the same: no verified study gives a dose-to-hormone link for germinating seeds, so the model adds none. Published growth effects of chronic gamma rays need several times the ISS dose rate, sustained over a whole life cycle (Vandenhove and colleagues).

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.800
A hypothesis, clearly marked

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:50.800
Right: what if radiation damage did signal? Three links are switched on: damage raises ABA, raises the ethylene precursor ACC, and slows cell division in the root tip.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:12.800
Root at 120 h: 3.4 mm without the links, 2.8 mm with them. Their strengths are assumed, so this shows the shape of a possible effect, not its size.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.800
What the data show: which cells respond

00:01:15.425 --> 00:01:24.425
This is data, not simulation: how strongly each cell type's marker genes are enriched for the response of young seedlings to simulated galactic cosmic rays, from the Seed Stress Decoder (manuscript in preparation).

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:32.800
Red: the radiation signature is enriched in that cell type. Blue: depleted. Grey: no matching cell type in the germination atlas.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.300
Magnetic fields: an open question

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:43.300
Earth's surface field is roughly 25 to 65 µT. The Moon's crustal field, mapped from orbit at 30 km, has a median of 0.75 nT.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:51.300
In one laboratory study (Dhiman, Wu and Galland, Protoplasma, 2023), a 50 µT field sped up Arabidopsis germination by about 20 h compared with a near-null field.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:59.300
Mutants lacking both cryptochromes (cry1cry2) responded the same way. With no known mechanism and no verified field values for the ISS, Mars or flight hardware, the seed twin does not model magnetic fields.
